Software Testing

.process of evaluating aa software app to verify that it works as expected and it meets specified requirements
.helps identify defects, errors, and missing functionalities before getting delivered to users 
.ensures reliability, security, and performance 




Types
    .Manual 
        .testers execute test cases manually without using automation tools
        .helps verify application functionality and identify defects by comparing actual results with expected results
            e.g manually checking whether a login page accepts valid credentials 

    
    .Automation 
        .test cases are executed using scripts and automation tools 
        .helps automate repetitive tasks, improving testing speed, accuracy, and efficiency
            e.g script automatically testing the login functionality and verifying the result 


    
Terms
    .test case - set of inputs, conditions, and expected results used to verify whether a specific functionality of the software works correctly
    .test suite - collection of multiple test cases grouped together to test different features of an application in various scenarios
    .test plan - document defining the scope, objectives, resources, schedule, and approach for testing activities
    .defects/bugs - errors or issues in the software where actual results differ from expected results, affecting functionality or performance
    .regression testing - testing performed after changes or updates to ensure existing features still work correctly and no new issues are introduced 


Common tools used 
    .Selenium: An open-source automation tool used for testing web applications. It supports multiple programming languages like Java, Python, and C#.
    .JIRA: A popular tool for bug tracking, issue management, and project tracking. It helps teams manage defects efficiently.
    .TestNG: A testing framework used with Selenium for organizing test cases, generating reports, and managing test execution.
    .Postman: A tool used for API testing. It allows testers to send requests, validate responses, and automate API tests.
    .LoadRunner: A performance testing tool used to simulate multiple users and analyze system behavior under load.
    .BrowserStack: A cloud-based testing platform used for cross-browser and cross-device testing of web and mobile applications. It allows testing on real browsers, operating systems, and mobile devices without requiring a local setup.


    